    { "file": "series-inspector.png", "tag": "auto-view", "referenced_from": ["client/graph.md"], "notes": "Trend workspace per-series inspector panel (SeriesInspector): colour swatches, display flags, limits, source. Reshell-only chrome, captured under --theme. Limits/quality populate because the capture makes the graphed node resident (FetchGraphNodesResident) before building the panel." },
    { "file": "device-diagnostics.png", "tag": "auto-view", "referenced_from": [], "notes": "Configuration workbench device-diagnostics inspector (DeviceDiagnostics): link-status hero (up/down/disabled) + live traffic/polling counters from the device's diagnostic child variables (Online/Enabled/MessagesIn/...). Reshell-only chrome (backlog 5.0), captured under --theme against a fixture device (TS.103, link down). Standalone like series-inspector; the capture makes the device resident (FetchNodesResident) so ShowDevice resolves the diagnostic variables and reads their current values. Not yet embedded in a manual page." },
    { "file": "users-rbac.png", "tag": "auto-view", "referenced_from": [], "notes": "Users-admin RBAC inspector (UserAccess): role pill (Administrator/Operator/Observer, derived from the user's AccessRights bitmask) + the three permission rows (view / control / configure) with granted state. Reshell-only chrome (backlog 5.1), captured under --theme against a fixture user (USER.5, AccessRights=3 = full Administrator). Standalone like device-diagnostics; the capture makes the user resident (FetchNodesResident) so ShowUser resolves UserType_AccessRights and reads its value. Not yet embedded in a manual page." },
    { "file": "transmission-rule.png", "tag": "auto-view", "referenced_from": [], "notes": "Transmission-rules editor inspector (TransmissionRule): the right region of transmission-rules.html for a selected transmission item — source signal + type tag (TS/TI), destination endpoint + IOA, and protocol (Modbus / IEC 60870-5-104 / IEC 61850, from the item's type). Reshell-only chrome (backlog 5.2), captured under --theme against a fixture rule (TS.733 TX_Ua → Modbus IOA 2001). Standalone like users-rbac; the capture makes the rule + its type chain, source and parent endpoint resident so ShowRule resolves the source/endpoint and reads SourceAddress. Read-only in this capture (no shell write path); the mockup's Trigger/Transform/Status/counters are server-side driver concepts absent from the client node model. Not yet embedded in a manual page." },
