    { "file": "limits-chart.png", "tag": "auto-view", "referenced_from": ["architecture.md"], "notes": "Graph with severity-coloured limit markers drawn (MetrixLine limit styles; TIT.200 carries AnalogItemType_LimitLoLo/Lo/Hi/HiHi in the fixture). SaveGraphScreenshot now makes each graphed node resident (FetchGraphNodesResident) before building the widget, so the node's EU range and limit-band property children are fetched: the axes use the EU range instead of the data auto-range and the limit markers draw. (The legend 'Current' cell stays blank in the offscreen fixture - the live monitored-item value is not delivered there, a separate gap that also blanks the write dialog's current value.)" },
